const [running, setRunning] = useState(false);
const [remaining, setRemaining] = useState(settings.focus * 60);
const endTimeRef = useRef(null);
const remainingRef = useRef(...);
```

Simpler approach: interval that ticks every 200ms while running. On tick: 
```
const now = Date.now();
const left = Math.max(0, endTimeRef.current - now) / 1000;
setRemaining(left);
if (left <= 0) complete();
```

When starting: `endTimeRef.current = Date.now() + remainingRef.current * 1000`.

Need remainingRef to mirror state for starting. Or use functional updates. I'll keep a ref synced.

On pause: setRunning(false), and remaining state holds current value (since we computed it in tick). But we should stop the interval. When we pause, capture the last computed remaining — the state already has it. Good.

